sequenceDiagram
    participant MQ as Main queue
    participant W as Consumer (worker)
    participant RQ as Retry queue
    participant DL as dead_letters (Postgres)
    participant DLQ as DLQ

    MQ->>W: deliver message (x-retry-count: 0)
    W->>W: handler throws
    W->>RQ: publish (x-retry-count: 1, expiration: ~1s)
    W->>MQ: ack original

    Note over RQ: message waits out its TTL
    RQ-->>MQ: dead-letters back on original routing key

    MQ->>W: redeliver (x-retry-count: 1)
    W->>W: handler throws again
    W->>RQ: publish (x-retry-count: 2, expiration: ~2s)
    W->>MQ: ack

    Note over RQ,MQ: repeats with exponential backoff<br/>(1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, ... capped at 60s)

    MQ->>W: redeliver (x-retry-count: maxRetries)
    W->>W: handler throws again — retries exhausted
    W->>DL: INSERT (queue, routing key, payload, error)
    W->>DLQ: publish final copy
    W->>MQ: ack original

    Note over DLQ: parked — nothing consumes automatically.<br/>Visible via the dead_letters table for manual triage.
